<%# THE TOP BAR'S UPLOAD (structural redesign spec §4.2 and §8, slice 4). It uploads into the folder
    the page shows (FolderDestination, set by that page's action) and says which.

    ONE BUTTON, TWO FLOWS — the Files page's own, moved here unchanged. `port_writable?` picks WHICH
    DOOR the bytes go in (CLAUDE.md §14a — it is not "can this deployment upload"; rendering the
    wrong one ships a button whose door answers 501), and both carry the destination as the
    `parent_node_id` the doors already accept.

    A ZIP HOLDING A MODEL FILE UNPACKS (2026-10-21; docs/superpowers/specs/
    2026-10-20-zip-upload-unpacks-models-design.md): both flows carry the two unpack doors and the
    server's model extensions, and lib/zip_unpack.js does the rest in the browser.

    A PAGE WITH NO FOLDER (Recent, Tools, Settings, Search) asks with the library's folder chooser
    before the file picker opens (upload_pick_controller.js), and never guesses one. Its targets are
    the two places the two flows read their destination from: the form's hidden field, or the chunk
    uploader's own parent value.

    `primary` only where Upload IS the screen's one action (design-system.md rule 13): the Library,
    the project hub and Recent — the last with no folder, so it still asks (FolderDestination's
    upload_primary?). The caption hides below 1100px, so the button's title carries it there. %>
<% dest = folder_destination %>
<% parent_value = dest ? dest.node_id.to_s : "" %>
<% btn_class = upload_primary? ? "upload-btn primary" : "upload-btn" %>
<% btn_title = dest ? "Saves to #{dest.caption}" : "Choose a folder, then files" %>
<% pick = dest.nil? %>
<%= tag.div class: "topbar-upload",
            data: (pick ? { controller: "upload-pick",
                            upload_pick_children_url_value: library_children_path,
                            upload_pick_create_url_value: library_folders_path } : {}) do %>
  <% if capabilities.port_writable? %>
    <%# Share/S3: no chunk store to presign into, so the bytes come up in one multipart POST. %>
    <%# THE ZIP-UPLOAD CONTROLLER (2026-10-21) submits this form exactly as the inline `onchange` it
        replaced did, for every selection without a model zip; a selection holding one is unpacked
        in the browser instead (zip_upload_controller.js, lib/zip_unpack.js). %>
    <%= form_with url: files_path, method: :post, class: "uploader",
                  data: { turbo: false, controller: "zip-upload",
                          zip_upload_create_url_value: files_path,
                          zip_upload_unpack_url_value: files_unpack_folder_path,
                          zip_upload_unpacked_url_value: files_unpacked_path,
                          zip_upload_model_exts_value: Maker::FileAttachment::MODEL_EXTS },
                  html: { multipart: true } do |f| %>
      <%= hidden_field_tag :parent_node_id, parent_value, id: nil,
                           data: { zip_upload_target: "parent", upload_pick_target: ("parent" if pick) } %>
      <%= tag.label class: btn_class, title: btn_title,
                    data: (pick ? { action: "click->upload-pick#pick" } : {}) do %>
        <%# `include_hidden: false` IS LOAD-BEARING. `f.file_field` with `multiple: true` renders a
            companion `<input name="file[]" type="hidden" value="">` so an empty selection still
            submits the key, which put a bare "" at the head of `params[:file]`, and the server
            called `original_filename` on a String and 500'd. Nothing needs that marker here: the
            field's own change handler is the only thing that submits this form, so it never fires
            with an empty selection. Found by uploading four real files through the real form; the
            Rack::Test suites POSTed a Ruby array and never sent the marker at all, which is §14d's
            "assert the rendered field name" with a different attribute (upload_batch_test.rb). %>
        <%= f.file_field :file, multiple: true, include_hidden: false, id: "topbar_upload_file", hidden: true,
                         data: { zip_upload_target: "input", action: "change->zip-upload#change",
                                 upload_pick_target: ("input" if pick) } %>
        <span>Upload</span>
      <% end %>
      <span class="upload-status" data-zip-upload-target="status"></span>
    <% end %>
  <% else %>
    <%# Chunk: the browser hashes, we presign the missing chunks, the browser PUTs them (§15). The
        section is built with `tag.section` so its optional `uploader` target is an attribute the
        builder writes, never a string spliced into an open tag. %>
    <%= tag.section class: "uploader",
                    data: { controller: "uploader",
                            uploader_begin_url_value: begin_upload_files_path,
                            uploader_finalize_url_value: finalize_upload_files_path,
                            uploader_parent_node_id_value: parent_value,
                            uploader_unpack_url_value: files_unpack_folder_path,
                            uploader_unpacked_url_value: files_unpacked_path,
                            uploader_model_exts_value: Maker::FileAttachment::MODEL_EXTS,
                            upload_pick_target: ("uploader" if pick) } do %>
      <%= tag.label class: btn_class, title: btn_title,
                    data: (pick ? { action: "click->upload-pick#pick" } : {}) do %>
        <%= tag.input type: "file", multiple: true, id: "topbar_upload_file", hidden: true,
                      data: { uploader_target: "input", action: "uploader#upload",
                              upload_pick_target: ("input" if pick) } %>
        <span>Upload</span>
      <% end %>
      <span class="upload-status" data-uploader-target="status"></span>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
  <% if dest %>
    <span class="topbar-upload-caption">Saves to <strong><%= dest.caption %></strong></span>
  <% else %>
    <span class="topbar-upload-caption" data-upload-pick-target="caption" hidden></span>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
